# dist/ is COMMITTED on purpose.
#
# It is build output, and normally that would be ignored. But it is also the
# only folder Chrome can load, and gitignoring it meant a fresh clone had
# exactly one folder containing a manifest.json -- extension/ -- which is the
# one that does not work. That produced the same opaque "status code 3" report
# twice. A committed dist/ makes the working path the discoverable one.
#
# It is rebuilt and verified by `npm run build`, and CI checks it is current.
